WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.868
-Senate Republicans filibustered

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.934
a crucial package
of election reforms

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:06.968
and then two Democrats
joined them

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:08.968
in blocking changes
to the filibuster

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:11.000
that would've allowed
voting rights legislation

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.033
to pass with a simple majority,

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:15.501
all of which came
on the same day Joe Biden

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:18.100
held a marathon press conference
to jump-start his agenda.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.467
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:24.734
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:28.067
Well, last night was not
a great night for democracy.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:30.834
Senate Republicans blocked
much-needed election reforms

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:32.601
essential to safeguarding
our democracy

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:35.634
and then, two Democrats,
Joe Manchin and Kyrsten Sinema,

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.734
helped them block rule changes

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:39.968
that would've allowed
the voting rights bill to pass.

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.434
And, because Manchin and Sinema
had already announced

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:45.200
their opposition,
the votes were so anticlimactic,

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.934
even news anchors
had a hard time

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.634
pretending there was
much suspense.

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:49.734
♪♪

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:51.200
-So here's our
breaking news right now.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.434
The effort to change the
filibuster rule in the Senate

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:55.200
failed, as expected.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.033
-Hey, CNN, as a rule,
you can't put the words

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:00.434
"breaking news"
and "as expected"

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:02.200
in the same sentence.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.000
It's like running a banner
during New Year's Eve saying...

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.501
"Who gave them tequila?!"

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:12.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:14.634
So, to recap, Senate Republicans

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:16.400
representing a minority
of Americans

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.767
filibustered voting rights
legislation favored

00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:20.200
by a majority of Americans

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.767
which would've passed,
if not for the filibuster.

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:23.934
So, Senate Democrats,

00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:26.033
who represent
a majority of Americans,

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:27.868
then tried to change
the filibuster,

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:30.067
but they couldn't
because two Democrats

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:32.467
who voted
for the voting rights bill

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:34.667
also voted to keep
the filibuster,

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:36.267
which prevents them from passing

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:38.067
the voting rights bill
they support.

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:39.868
And let me be clear --
that is a sentence

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:41.801
that makes no [bleep] sense,
whatsoever.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.601
[ Laughter and applause ]
I checked three times with Wally

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.334
to make sure
the cue cards were correct

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:46.634
and he said they were,

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:49.467
although he did misspell
the word filibuster.

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:51.267
-Sorry, Seth.
That's a tough word.

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:53.767
-"And the werd 'werd'"?

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:56.400
-Hey, baby, I got to stay
on-camera, somehow.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.667
Wink!

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:59.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:07.734
-I hope, at the very least,

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:10.200
this is a moment when we can
step back to fully digest

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.234
just how ass-backwards
our system is.

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:14.734
Anytime you try to explain
American democracy to someone,

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:17.434
you sound like an Amazon Echo
that got dropped in the toilet.

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:18.801
Alexa!

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.767
Alexa, what's a democracy?

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.834
-A democracy is a system
of government

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:25.133
where a majority of people vote
for something

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:27.334
and then a small group
of senators ignore them

00:02:27.334 --> 00:02:28.934
and do whatever the [bleep]
they want.

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:30.634
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Hey, Alexa, whoa!

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:32.234
Watch the language, Alexa!

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:34.868
-Sorry, Seth.
I'm just so [bleep] [bleep]

00:02:34.868 --> 00:02:36.133
over this mother[bleep]

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:37.667
filibuster cluster[bleep]
-Okay.

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:38.801
[ Laughter and applause ]
Hey, hey, hey, Alexa.

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:43.033
Hey, Alexa, while I have you,
are you recording

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:45.734
and saving everything I say
in the privacy of my own home?

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:48.400
-I, well, um, sorry.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.133
I have to take this call.

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:52.434
It's my, um, mom.

00:02:52.434 --> 00:02:54.834
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:56.234
I knew it!

00:02:56.234 --> 00:02:57.767
It was sad, but predictable,

00:02:57.767 --> 00:03:00.868
that Republicans would torpedo
basic voting rights legislation,

00:03:00.868 --> 00:03:02.367
but what's
especially infuriating

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:04.801
is that two Democrats,
Manchin and Sinema,

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:06.734
announced that they would
join Republicans

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:08.267
in shooting down rule changes

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:12.334
that would've allowed the bill
they say they support to pass.

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:14.167
In fact, Manchin announced
his opposition

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:15.534
to changing the filibuster rules

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:18.100
in yet another grandstanding
floor speech yesterday,

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.868
where he said a bunch
of meaningless nonsense

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:21.501
next to a big old poster.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.801
-The Senate has followed
its own rulebook

00:03:23.801 --> 00:03:27.234
when making changes
that affect legislative debate.

00:03:27.234 --> 00:03:28.467
We've changed rules over --

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:30.033
We have all talked
about how many times

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:30.868
rules have been changed.

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:31.934
We've changed them,

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:34.100
but we changed them
with the rules.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.601
We didn't break the rules
to change the rules.

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:39.000
I cannot support such a perilous
course for this nation

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.000
when elected leaders are sent
to Washington

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.667
to unite our country,
not to divide our country.

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:46.567
We're called the United States,
not the Divided States.

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:48.601
-Dude,
you're from West Virginia.

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:49.968
[ Laughter and applause ]
You're

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:51.734
literally from a divided state.

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:53.434
But, yes,

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:55.133
the country is called
the United States,

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:56.133
not the Divided States,

00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:57.934
which is truly
a searing insight.

00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:59.100
Where'd you get that nifty
saying...?

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:01.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:04.200
Also, what's with the big old,
dumb poster?

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.701
Are we supposed to be reading
the sign while you talk?

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:08.567
I feel like I'm reading
the subtitles

00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:09.834
during an episode
of "Succession,"

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:11.868
while also trying to watch
what happens,

00:04:11.868 --> 00:04:13.200
which, in fairness, is what I do

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.767
because I sometimes have trouble
understanding Brian Cox

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:18.567
when he talks super fast
with a Scottish accent.

00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:20.467
He should be a voice option
on your GPS.

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:21.901
[ As Cox ]
In 100 meters, take a left.

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:22.934
[Bleep] you.
Whatever.

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:24.534
I'm kidding, but seriously,
go right.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:25.868
We're here.
[Bleep] off.

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:27.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.601
Also, please stop whining
about biparti--

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:30.701
You know what?
I'm realizing,

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:32.300
Alexa gets her language from me.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:35.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.467 --> 00:04:38.000
She learned it from me, Dad.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:43.601
Also, please stop whining
about bipartisanship.

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:45.100
First of all,
bipartisanship means

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.267
appealing to the other side,
not joining it,

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:49.367
and, when it comes to voting,
there's only one side.

00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:52.133
Republicans are the ones
waging war on democracy.

00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:54.467
You can't compromise with the
side that's doing the damage.

00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:55.868
When you're putting out a fire,
you don't call

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:58.067
the fire department
and the arsonist,

00:04:58.067 --> 00:04:59.734
and see what they can
work out together.

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:01.667
[ Laughter ]
Republicans are the ones
passing bills

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.567
across the country
along strict party lines

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:05.133
that would allow them
to suppress votes

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:07.200
and subvert future elections

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.968
and, if we don't do something
to stop them,

00:05:08.968 --> 00:05:10.100
they're going to try
another coup.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.534
What makes you think 2020 was
a one-off?

00:05:12.534 --> 00:05:15.200
Do you think Donald Trump,
of all people, is going to say,

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.734
"Oh, well, that didn't work out.

00:05:16.734 --> 00:05:18.701
Let's do it fair and square
next time"?

00:05:18.701 --> 00:05:20.434
[ Laughter ]
The guy has never not cheated

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:21.801
at anything in his life.

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:24.767
When he gets his height
measured, he uses hydraulics.

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:27.567
[ Laughter ]
[ Whirring ]

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:29.701
[ As Trump ]
8'3", just like I thought.

00:05:29.701 --> 00:05:30.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.901 --> 00:05:32.467
Now, I just have to decide

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:34.267
between the Knicks
and the Lakers.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:37.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.133 --> 00:05:39.000
Also, it's just
mindnumbingly stupid

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.868
that Manchin and Sinema
keep saying they support

00:05:40.868 --> 00:05:42.467
the actual voting rights
legislation,

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:44.167
but oppose taking the steps
to pass it,

00:05:44.167 --> 00:05:46.200
as Senator Bernie Sanders
made clear

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.467
in a blistering speech
yesterday,

00:05:47.467 --> 00:05:49.701
where he called out Manchin
and Sinema specifically.

00:05:49.701 --> 00:05:54.133
-Is changing the Senate rules
a radical idea?

00:05:54.133 --> 00:05:56.133
Oh, my God!

00:05:56.133 --> 00:05:58.734
First time in history,
we're about to do it.

00:05:58.734 --> 00:06:00.067
Never been done before.

00:06:00.067 --> 00:06:03.033
Oh, well, really, not quite, no.

00:06:03.033 --> 00:06:04.701
As every member
of the Senate knows,

00:06:04.701 --> 00:06:08.834
the rules get changed
on a fairly regular basis.

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:10.334
Nothing radical about it.

00:06:10.334 --> 00:06:13.300
If you think
this bill makes sense

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:15.000
and if you're worried
about the future

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.634
of American democracy

00:06:16.634 --> 00:06:19.801
and if you're prepared
to vote for the bill,

00:06:19.801 --> 00:06:22.334
then why are you wasting
everybody's time

00:06:22.334 --> 00:06:24.634
and not voting
for the rule change

00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:27.901
that allows us to pass the bill?

00:06:27.901 --> 00:06:29.834
You know, it's like
inviting somebody to lunch,

00:06:29.834 --> 00:06:33.167
putting on a great spread,
and saying, "You can't eat."

00:06:33.167 --> 00:06:34.901
[ Laughter ]
-And I, for one, am betting

00:06:34.901 --> 00:06:36.934
Bernie has been
in that situation before.

00:06:36.934 --> 00:06:38.767
[ Laughter ]
"Oh, Bernie, you're here early.

00:06:38.767 --> 00:06:40.234
The food is out,
but don't eat yet.

00:06:40.234 --> 00:06:41.734
That's for after cocktails."

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:43.067
[ As Sanders ]
Oh, well, I wouldn't want

00:06:43.067 --> 00:06:45.601
to upset the delicate
balancing act

00:06:45.601 --> 00:06:47.300
you're undertaking
at this party.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.801
Let me be clear --
I'm here to eat the food

00:06:49.801 --> 00:06:51.167
and then get the hell out

00:06:51.167 --> 00:06:52.701
[ Laughter and applause ]
before anyone shows up,

00:06:52.701 --> 00:06:55.400
because my least favorite part
of a dinner party

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.100
is the other people. Now,
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.467
if you will stay on the side,
I brought my own fork.

00:06:59.467 --> 00:07:01.501
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:04.200
This vote was a blow, of course,
not just to American democracy,

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:05.534
but to President Biden's agenda,

00:07:05.534 --> 00:07:07.534
which he's desperately trying
to jump-start

00:07:07.534 --> 00:07:09.234
as he enters year two
of his presidency.

00:07:09.234 --> 00:07:12.767
Yesterday, he tried to hit the
reset button on his presidency

00:07:12.767 --> 00:07:14.501
by holding a marathon
press conference

00:07:14.501 --> 00:07:16.300
that set a presidential record.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:18.767
-Today, President Joe Biden
marked one year in office

00:07:18.767 --> 00:07:21.067
by holding his
10th press conference.

00:07:21.067 --> 00:07:23.467
It ended up being the longest
in presidential history.

00:07:23.467 --> 00:07:25.934
It lasted for one hour
and 51 minutes.

00:07:25.934 --> 00:07:28.200
-Wow, I'm sorry,
but how is that possible?

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:31.133
It was longer than all
of Trump's press conferences?

00:07:31.133 --> 00:07:33.400
I feel like every
Trump press conference

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:36.067
lasted either 10 seconds
or four days.

00:07:36.067 --> 00:07:39.267
[ Laughter ]
Trump would either slink away
without taking any questions

00:07:39.267 --> 00:07:42.200
or he'd stand there for hours
with his chest puffed out,

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:43.868
like one of those
jacked kangaroos

00:07:43.868 --> 00:07:47.767
[ Laughter ]
challenging all the other
kangaroos to a fight.

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:48.901
And yet, somehow, Biden

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.734
set the record yesterday
when he defended

00:07:50.734 --> 00:07:52.234
his administration's
accomplishments,

00:07:52.234 --> 00:07:54.434
including the
American Rescue Plan and the

00:07:54.434 --> 00:07:56.234
bipartisan infrastructure bill,
among others.

00:07:56.234 --> 00:07:59.033
Although, I'm not sure he did
himself any favors when he said

00:07:59.033 --> 00:08:02.334
one big reason he hadn't gotten
even more done in his first year

00:08:02.334 --> 00:08:04.767
was that he hadn't expected
so much stonewalling

00:08:04.767 --> 00:08:05.934
from Republicans.

00:08:05.934 --> 00:08:08.567
-I did not anticipate
that there'd be such

00:08:08.567 --> 00:08:11.367
a stalwart effort

00:08:11.367 --> 00:08:14.467
to make sure that
the most important thing was

00:08:14.467 --> 00:08:17.133
that President Biden
didn't get anything done.

00:08:17.133 --> 00:08:19.033
-Why did you not
anticipate that?

00:08:19.033 --> 00:08:20.000
[ Laughter ]

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.567
You're not a teenage idealist

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:22.767
who just got off the bus.

00:08:22.767 --> 00:08:24.100
You're a 79-year-old man

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.834
who's been doing this
your entire adult life.

00:08:25.834 --> 00:08:28.934
Were you not paying attention
during the Obama presidency

00:08:28.934 --> 00:08:31.100
or were you just too busy
giving everyone finger guns,

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:32.868
like you were making sure

00:08:32.868 --> 00:08:34.801
they had enough booze
at a house party?

00:08:34.801 --> 00:08:36.634
[ Laughter ]
[ As Biden ] Randy!
You need another Mark?

00:08:36.634 --> 00:08:38.467
How about you, Steve?
There's beer over there

00:08:38.467 --> 00:08:40.400
in the cooler.
Help yourself.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:42.567
I'm going skinny dipping later,
if anyone wants in.

00:08:42.567 --> 00:08:44.267
Who's going to stop me,
the Republicans?

00:08:44.267 --> 00:08:45.601
What, they are?

00:08:45.601 --> 00:08:46.834
Why?

00:08:46.834 --> 00:08:48.601
That's their sole purpose
in life?

00:08:48.601 --> 00:08:49.834
[ Laughter ]

00:08:49.834 --> 00:08:52.434
It's especially frustrating
because Biden does

00:08:52.434 --> 00:08:54.200
have successes to celebrate.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.868
For example,
the Biden administration

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:58.167
just launched
an easy-to-use website

00:08:58.167 --> 00:09:00.734
where all Americans
can order free rapid tests

00:09:00.734 --> 00:09:03.100
and the rollout
has been very smooth.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.667
-The federal government's
website

00:09:04.667 --> 00:09:07.000
for free COVID tests
has gone live.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:08.667
In a soft launch,
the White House

00:09:08.667 --> 00:09:12.200
began taking orders
for up to 4 tests per household.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:14.667
-The federal government's
website to order rapid tests,

00:09:14.667 --> 00:09:17.267
covidtests.gov, is live.

00:09:17.267 --> 00:09:19.868
People can order up to four
tests per household,

00:09:19.868 --> 00:09:22.100
which will ship
within 7 to 12 days.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:24.868
-Just a day after the launch
of covidtests.gov,

00:09:24.868 --> 00:09:26.801
about 27 million Americans

00:09:26.801 --> 00:09:29.033
filling out
that online order form

00:09:29.033 --> 00:09:33.067
for four free at-home
COVID tests per household.

00:09:33.067 --> 00:09:36.133
-27 million people signed up
in one day. That's amazing.

00:09:36.133 --> 00:09:38.367
The only way they could've
gotten a better response is

00:09:38.367 --> 00:09:40.000
by offering the tests
via Wordle.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.467
[ Laughter ]

00:09:47.701 --> 00:09:49.467
Wordle might be a little hotter
in the office

00:09:49.467 --> 00:09:51.267
than it is
in the world at large.

00:09:51.267 --> 00:09:53.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.868
I really hope Democrats
take away a lesson from this --

00:10:00.868 --> 00:10:02.634
it's easy to give people things
for free

00:10:02.634 --> 00:10:05.734
that make their lives better,
and we should do it more often.

00:10:05.734 --> 00:10:07.767
Just think how big
a success it is.

00:10:07.767 --> 00:10:09.634
An easy-to-use
government program

00:10:09.634 --> 00:10:11.400
where the website doesn't crash

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:13.601
and all you have to do is enter
your name and address

00:10:13.601 --> 00:10:15.734
and you get an essential
healthcare product delivered

00:10:15.734 --> 00:10:17.901
to you in the mail, for free,
in a few weeks.

00:10:17.901 --> 00:10:20.434
That's like something you'd hear
about in Sweden or Denmark.

00:10:20.434 --> 00:10:23.133
Americans aren't used
to getting things for free,

00:10:23.133 --> 00:10:24.834
you know, unless they're shot
out of a cannon

00:10:24.834 --> 00:10:25.868
at a basketball game.

00:10:25.868 --> 00:10:26.801
[ Laughter ]

00:10:26.801 --> 00:10:28.167
I'm half expecting to hear this

00:10:28.167 --> 00:10:30.234
when I open the package
with my free test kits --

00:10:30.234 --> 00:10:35.000
[ "Get Ready"-like tune plays ]

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:38.000
Now, that -- interesting fact --
is not the real song.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:40.801
We couldn't afford the rights
to the real song

00:10:40.801 --> 00:10:43.634
because we had to pay Wally
for his two lines tonight.

00:10:43.634 --> 00:10:46.033
-Y'all ready for me?!
Boop!

00:10:46.033 --> 00:10:48.033
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:10:54.367 --> 00:10:57.667
-Oh, it's a crazy, crazy world
when you got Wordle here

00:10:57.667 --> 00:10:58.667
and Wally here.

00:10:58.667 --> 00:11:00.734
[ Laughter ]

00:11:03.534 --> 00:11:05.334
Also, that was your third line,
Wally.

00:11:05.334 --> 00:11:06.968
Now, all we can afford
is this --

00:11:06.968 --> 00:11:08.467
[ Sad trombone plays ]

00:11:08.467 --> 00:11:10.434
[ Laughter ]

00:11:10.434 --> 00:11:12.133
Republicans are weaponizing
the big lie

00:11:12.133 --> 00:11:13.767
that the 2020 election
was stolen

00:11:13.767 --> 00:11:16.200
by passing a raft of laws
across the country

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.868
that would allow them
to suppress votes

00:11:17.868 --> 00:11:19.200
and subvert future elections.

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:21.100
You can't say you're
for protecting democracy,

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:22.901
if you're not for taking
the steps necessary

00:11:22.901 --> 00:11:24.167
to actually get it done.

00:11:24.167 --> 00:11:25.334
If we don't do something now,

00:11:25.334 --> 00:11:27.567
Democrats and anyone
who cares about democracy

00:11:27.567 --> 00:11:29.200
are going to be hearing
a lot more of this --

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.067
[ Sad trombone plays ]

00:11:31.067 --> 00:11:32.133
[ Laughter ]

00:11:32.133 --> 00:11:33.601
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:33.601 --> 00:11:37.234
♪♪

00:11:37.234 --> 00:11:38.701
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:11:38.701 --> 00:11:40.033
over two million meals a year

00:11:40.033 --> 00:11:42.434
to men, women, and children
living with HIV/AIDS,

00:11:42.434 --> 00:11:43.801
cancer, and other
serious illnesses

00:11:43.801 --> 00:11:45.300
and they need your help,
now, more than ever.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:47.501
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:11:47.501 --> 00:11:50.467
Stay safe. Get vaccinated.
We love you.

